Result shapes are validated in source-position order across provider classes, so the
concrete provider's multiple-error rejection at the earlier position fires, not the later
template's bare-type-parameter rejection. Validating templates first would report Worse
here even though Bad comes first in the file.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrMultipleErrors
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

//plumb:build
func Bad() (int, error, error) { return 0, nil, nil }

//plumb:build
func Worse[T any]() T { var z T; return z }
